POWER AUTOMATE FLOW STATUS
Flow name: Activity Log Processing

FLOW OVERALL STRUCTURE
1. Trigger: SharePoint — When an item is created
2. First Update item action:
   - sets Workflow Status = In Progress
   - sets Excel Logged = No
   - passes through other mapped fields
3. First Condition:
   - compares Activity Type Value to Direct Service
   - True branch = Direct_Hours logging
   - False branch goes to second condition
4. Second Condition inside first False branch:
   - compares Activity Type Value to Indirect Service
   - True branch = Indirect_Hours logging
   - False branch = Supervision logging
5. Each branch has:
   - Add a row into Excel table
   - Final Update item action
6. Final Update item actions set:
   - Workflow Status = Complete
   - Excel Logged = Yes

IMPORTANT FLOW CORRECTIONS ALREADY DISCOVERED
1. The left side of conditions must use:
   - When an item is created → Activity Type Value
2. The right side of condition text must use exact SharePoint choice text:
   - Direct Service
   - Indirect Service
3. Table names are NOT used in conditions
4. Excel table names ARE used only in Add a row into a table actions:
   - Direct_Hours
   - Indirect_Hours
   - Supervision

